{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","text":"Hypergraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Edges.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Edge position ","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is incidence number ","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the incidences hyperedge by hyperedge, in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index order, and within a hyperedge in ","type":"text"},{"code":"memberIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. So ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[q]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedEdge(i, n + p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the rows of the hyperedge side are contiguous ranges, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array (a weight of a vertex in a hyperedge) is indexed by edge position. A view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a snapshot, so its own positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until its next mutation: the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one), and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array must be rebuilt for it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The LabeledGraph law."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Every index member reads the base’s rows:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"type":"text","text":" shifted by n, and of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" it is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)"},{"type":"text","text":". So "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traversal"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Connectivity"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ShortestPaths"},{"type":"text","text":" and the rest run on the view without hashing a vertex. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withIncidentIndexRows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes the view’s rows out once per call from the base’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withIncidenceRows"},{"type":"text","text":", in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(n + m + p), so whole-graph algorithms (components, bridges, cut vertices) run at an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"adjacency-list copy’s speed on every base."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Costs.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The view keeps each hyperedge’s first incidence number, so a hyperedge’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" is a range, O(1). On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":", which stores its incidences,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every read is O(1) plus the row. On any other base, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binary-search the hyperedge and find the member by its rank ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberIndex(atRank:…)"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" and O(log m + k) by default, and a vertex’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" finds its place in each of its hyperedges: O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which counts bits, and O(Σ k) over them on a base without a faster "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberRank"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BipartiteGraph(h.incidenceGraph, left: 0 ..< h.vertexCount)"},{"text":" gives the bipartite structure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the view’s components restricted to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n"},{"text":" are the hypergraph’s.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"IncidenceGraphView.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView.swift#L50"},"roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:11Hypergraphs18IncidenceGraphViewV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"Hypergraphs"}],"title":"IncidenceGraphView","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView"},"abstract":[{"text":"An undirected hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0 ..< n + m","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose vertex ","type":"text"},{"code":"i < n","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex index ","type":"text"},{"code":"i","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and whose vertex ","type":"text"},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is hyperedge ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with an edge ","type":"text"},{"code":"{i, n + p}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for each incidence. It is bipartite and simple","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(vertices on the left, hyperedges on the right), an empty hyperedge is an isolated vertex, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it loses nothing.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Edges-swift.struct","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/IncidentEdgeIndices","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Neighbors"],"title":"Structures","generated":true},{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/init(base:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/I